# Netlify redirects

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Sprint 2 trilingual roots — staged 2026-05-03
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These rules redirect legacy root URLs to their /en/ or /fr/ equivalents
# (depending on D4/D5 source-of-truth mapping). They are STAGED, not yet
# active: Netlify resolves existing static files before _redirects rules,
# so as long as /about.html, /compare.html, etc. still exist at the repo
# root, those legacy URLs continue to be served unchanged.
#
# The rules will become live in a later commit when the legacy root files
# are removed (after exhaustive deploy-preview validation + header.js /
# footer.js lang-aware updates landed).
#
# Query strings: preserved via :splat where useful (e.g. compare.html?c=).
# 301! (with bang) = force redirect even if a file exists at the source.
#
# Source of truth: see MIGRATION_PLAN.md §3 (Redirect Plan) and §1.1 (D4/D5).

# ───── ROOT (default lang = EN) ─────
/                                /en/                              301!
/index.html                      /en/                              301!

# ───── EN-source pages → /en/ ─────
/about.html                      /en/about.html                    301!
# /compare.html: bare-URL rule MUST come before the splat — Netlify's *
# requires at least one char after the path, so without this line the bare
# /compare.html falls through to the source file (200 instead of 301).
# The splat rule below catches /compare.html?c=... query string variants
# (Netlify preserves the query via :splat).
/compare.html                    /en/compare.html                  301!
/compare.html *                  /en/compare.html?:splat           301!
/globe.html                      /en/globe.html                    301!
/indexchronicles.html            /en/indexchronicles.html          301!
/terms.html                      /en/terms.html                    301!
/privacy.html                    /en/privacy.html                  301!
/confirmation.html               /en/confirmation.html             301!

# ───── FR-source pages → /fr/ ─────
/chronicles-villes.html          /fr/chronicles-villes.html        301!
/chronicles-dest.html            /fr/chronicles-dest.html          301!
/chronicles-family.html          /fr/chronicles-family.html        301!
/chronicles-horizons.html        /fr/chronicles-horizons.html      301!
/chronicles-visas.html           /fr/chronicles-visas.html         301!

# ───── wiggmatch — temporary FR-only (D1: dedicated trilingual sprint TBD) ─────
/wiggmatch.html                  /fr/wiggmatch.html                301!

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Pre-existing rules (kept)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Old dynamic country URL → new static page (default to English)
# JS lang switcher will redirect to the user's preferred language afterwards.
/countries/country.html  country=:slug  /countries/:slug-en.html  301!
